# web-music-visualizer

an in-browser music visualization experiment mostly developed around 2023

entirely locally processes music and plays it with programmatic visuals, like Windows Media Player or Milkdrop but in the browser and with code you can mess with

note that the user interface is still a work in progress, so things may be a bit rough around the edges

this is powered by my [musIQ](https://github.com/benjamingwynn/musIQ) library

live demo available at https://musiq-testing.netlify.app/

netlify automatically builds and publishes the repo from the `production` branch

this does not do any external communication, once you've opened the webpage and musiq's models have been loaded onto your machine, that's it. there is no server, no telemetry, no tracking.

### instructions

the program contains a list of music visualizations ready to use, simply add your music and pick a visualization and the visuals _should_ move _vaguely_ in sync with the music

Chrome works best

you can open the code of the visualization by pressing the "c" button on your keyboard. you can entirely change the visual like this, and experiment with the rest of the code, or even add an entire new visual

the "dots and lines" provided visualization is recreation of [spotify starfield](https://github.com/benjamingwynn/spotifystarfield.com) in WebGPU and is in my opinion the strongest one, this being the effective spiritual successor to that project. other examples are provided by me and some AIs, with mixed results

other key binds:
- `k` play/pause
- `j` previous track
- `l` next track
- `n` next visualization
- `p` previous visualization
- `o` open the file picker
- `f` toggle fullscreen
- `esc` open library view

### building

- npm i
- npm start (OR) npm run build
